<title>BRAZIL: Brazil TAM up 5.9 pct in morning trade.</title>
<headline>Brazil TAM up 5.9 pct in morning trade.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preferred shares of Brazilian airline TAM recouped some of Thursday's heavy losses and rose 5.9 percent to 53.50 reais this morning on the Sao Paulo bourse, brokers said.</p>
<p>TAM shares had plunged 22.3 percent on Thursday following an accident involving a Fokker-100 aircraft operated by the airline which killed 104 people.</p>
<p>The plane crashed into homes in a densely populated area of Sao Paulo shortly after taking off from Congonhas regional airport.</p>
<p>The Bovespa index was 0.78 percent higher at 65,898 points.</p>
<p>-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
